&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Disclaimer:&lt;/strong&gt; The following &lt;span style=&quot;color: green&quot;&gt;FILE&lt;/span&gt; discusses semiohazards and their properties.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;quot;&lt;em&gt;A semiohazard, informally, is a fact of the universe that just shouldn&#039;t be true, but functionally is. They are inherently abstract and affect the way that we think and communicate about reality.&lt;/em&gt;&amp;quot;&lt;sup class=&quot;footnoteref&quot;&gt;&lt;a id=&quot;footnoteref-628988-1&quot; href=&quot;javascript:;&quot; class=&quot;footnoteref&quot;  &gt;1&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A particularly costly example of one such fact is, &amp;quot;The operations of &#039;YWTGTSYT&#039; are &lt;a target=&quot;_blank&quot; href=&quot;http://www.scp-wiki.net/scp-4703&quot;&gt;perfectly legal&lt;/a&gt;,&amp;quot; which is currently requiring the Foundation Legal Department to entirely redraft Texas corporate law&lt;sup class=&quot;footnoteref&quot;&gt;&lt;a id=&quot;footnoteref-628988-2&quot; href=&quot;javascript:;&quot; class=&quot;footnoteref&quot;  &gt;2&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/sup&gt;. Such things are facts of baseline reality; they always have been, and always will be, true. But they &lt;em&gt;shouldn&#039;t&lt;/em&gt;, and we &lt;em&gt;know&lt;/em&gt; they shouldn&#039;t. They aren&#039;t part of reality because reality says so, but because reality has been pulled inside-out by the conceptual nature of semantic equivalence itself. Alas, there is nothing we can do but reframe our definition of baseline and move on. To purposely poke at the bugs in the simulation is to invite a crash.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Read on, knowing that you must accept what the universe says is true, even if it doesn&#039;t make sense. One plus one doesn&#039;t always equal two.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: right;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;- Director Eli Forkley, Dept. of Miscommunications&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
